"""Builds this service's logger and owns the log schema.

The name shadows nothing: absolute imports mean `import logging` elsewhere
still finds the standard library, and this package is
`{@ package_name @}.internal.logging`.

Belongs here: the processor chain that renders the two tiers (a human console
form for local development, one JSON object per line everywhere else), the
reserved-field block, trace correlation, redaction, and the bridge that pulls
third-party stdlib log records into the same shape.

Does NOT belong here: log call sites. Those live wherever the interesting
thing happened.

The field set is defined in `docs/logging.md` and nowhere else. Mint's
`make parity` boots a service in each language and diffs the emitted keys
against that document, so a field invented at a call site is a parity failure
rather than a nice extra.

Empty until Mint chunk 04. Until then the service prints one plain startup
line, and that is not a log record — do not build on it.
"""
